<section id="surface">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <span class="eyebrow">THE WAY IN</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Your Attack Surface</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">Three surfaces. Every one of them has a door someone on your team forgot to lock. I find it.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="services-grid">
    <div class="service-card reveal">
      <div class="svc-index mono">01 / WEB</div>
      <svg class="service-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="1" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/><path d="M3 9h18M8 9v11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/><circle cx="5.5" cy="6.5" r="0.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
      <h3>Web Applications</h3>
      <p>Your login flow. Your session logic. Your access controls. I don't run a scan and call it a day — I hunt for the assumption your developers made that turns out to be wrong.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="service-card reveal d1">
      <div class="svc-index mono">02 / API</div>
      <svg class="service-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/><path d="M12 3v18M3 12h18" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2.2" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
      <h3>APIs &amp; Microservices</h3>
      <p>The endpoints your frontend never calls. The trust between services nobody re-checks. IDOR, SSRF, broken authorization — the gaps that live exactly where no one is looking.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="service-card reveal d2">
      <div class="svc-index mono">03 / LOGIC</div>
      <svg class="service-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M12 2l8 4v6c0 5-3.5 8.5-8 10-4.5-1.5-8-5-8-10V6l8-4z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      <h3>Access Control &amp; Logic</h3>
      <p>The flaws no tool finds, because they need someone who understands what your system is supposed to do. Privilege escalation. Tenant isolation breaks. One request that shouldn't work — but does.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="killlog">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <span class="eyebrow">PROOF OF WORK</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Kill Log</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">Real vulnerabilities. Real production targets. Names redacted — the impact isn't.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="killlog">
    <div class="kl-entry reveal">
      <div class="kl-header">
        <span class="kl-sev sev-crit">CRITICAL</span>
        <span class="kl-target mono">target: <span class="redact">████████ · SaaS</span></span>
