        <div class="kl-desc">A zero-privilege account rewrote one field in a config endpoint and redirected the server's own outbound requests. Then the server started calling back on its own — no interaction needed — leaking signed provider credentials and reaching internal infrastructure through the redirect chain.</div>
        <div class="kl-result mono"><span class="kl-tag">IMPACT</span> automatic credential exfiltration + internal network access</div>
        <div class="kl-status mono"><span class="kl-dot"></span> reported · triaged · patched</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="kl-entry reveal d1">
